SM-T715 tablet: the Modem tile, over t715-modem-power.

The modem's own switch, next to Airplane mode in the catalogue and at the end
of the default layout: off powers the CP down and keeps it off across a
reboot, on boots it again (t715-modem-power, package t715-modem, through
polkit). A long press opens Réseau mobile, which also holds the modem's
standby setting (off with the screen). The Mobile data tile says "Modem off"
rather than "Set up" while the switch is off. tile-state.sh reads the switch's
JSON with the shell's own patterns -- no text output is parsed, so there is
no locale to pin down there (the nmcli probes of 0010 already run with
LC_ALL=C). test/tile-scripts.sh and test/tiles-model.js follow. Ported from
the armv7h series' 0011-tablet-modem-tile (omamobile-shell 0.2.94). Against
omarchy-mobile 8991845 (omamobile-shell 0.2.147), after 0001-0011; the
modemStatus() helper joins TilesModel.js next to dictationStatus() and is
exported like it, and the tile's backend sits in the stubs section beside
mobileData as in 0.2.94.

